    "id": "fig05a",
    "number": "5(a)",
    "title": "Figure 5. Variation with lift coefficient of the aerodynamic characteristics for the 10.8 deg sweptback wing. (a) Angle of attack.",
    "pdf_page": 21,
    "printed_page": 19,
    "x_axis": "Lift coefficient, C_L, on staggered scales. Common axis used here = the M = 0.50 scale: left frame line = -0.2, grid every 0.1, right frame line = 3.2 (35 vertical lines). The label row under the plot reads -.2 at the left frame, then one '0' per Mach number every 0.2 (M = 0.50, .70, .85, .90, .925, .95, .975, 1.00, 1.02, 1.035, 1.085, 1.10, 1.114), then .2, .4, .6, .8 (M = 1.114 scale, .8 at the right frame). Each '0' sits under a short tick at the bottom of its cell of the Mach-number box, and each tick continues a vertical grid line (checked against the traced lines: ticks at x = 500, 640, 779, 918, 1057, 1197, 1335, 1473, 1612, 1753, 1891, 2031, 2172 px, grid lines 0.0 to 2.4 at 502.6 to 2174.5 px on row 1160, the 2 to 3 px difference being the page skew). So CL = 0 is at common-axis 0.0 (M 0.50), 0.4 (0.85), 1.0 (0.95), 1.4 (1.00), 2.2 (1.10).",
    "y_axis": "Angle of attack, alpha, deg (grid -4 to 14 by 1; frame lines at -4 and 14). The alpha = -3 line is not printed: the strip between alpha = -3.2 and -4 holds the Mach-number box, drawn over erased grid, so that line is skipped and the bottom cell is interpolated between the -2 and -4 lines.",
    "content_note": "One hollow symbol shape with a centre dot per Mach number, on one faired line per Mach number. Same test points as figure 5(b)."
  },
